{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117314","id":3382694731,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7Jn9NL","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117314","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117314.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117314.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117314","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117314/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117314/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117314/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/2ffe41b5cebf88ed09419d2e2e2477639a73f321","number":117314,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"core/templates: add SPSCRing<T,SIZE> lock-free SPSC ring buffer","user":{"login":"Mattbusel","id":183046053,"node_id":"U_kgDOCukPpQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/183046053?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mattbusel","html_url":"https://github.com/Mattbusel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mattbusel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mattbusel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mattbusel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mattbusel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mattbusel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mattbusel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mattbusel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mattbusel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mattbusel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What this adds\n\n`core/templates/spsc_ring.h` — a `SPSCRing<T, SIZE>` template: a lock-free, zero-allocation ring buffer safe for exactly one producer thread and one consumer thread.\n\n## Why this is needed\n\nThe existing `RingBuffer<T>` (`core/templates/ring_buffer.h`) uses plain `int` indices with no synchronisation and is explicitly single-threaded. It cannot be safely used across threads.\n\nThe audio system works around this today with `AudioRBResampler`, which reimplements the SPSC pattern manually using `SafeNumeric<int>` — but that primitive is private to the resampler and cannot be reused.\n\n`SPSCRing` gives Godot a clean, reusable, formally correct SPSC primitive for any two-thread pipeline: audio command queues, network receive → decode, physics event feeds, etc.\n\n## Properties\n\n| Property | Detail |\n|---|---|\n| Lock-free | No `Mutex`, `BinaryMutex`, `Semaphore`, or spin-lock |\n| Zero heap allocation | Storage is a fixed inline `std::array` — `SIZE*sizeof(T) + 128` bytes total |\n| Cache-friendly | `tail_` and `head_` on separate `alignas(64)` cache lines, eliminating false sharing between producer and consumer |\n| noexcept | `push`/`pop` never throw provided T satisfies noexcept move requirements |\n| Non-blocking | `push()` returns `false` when full; `pop()` returns `false` and leaves the output unchanged when empty |\n| MSVC-compatible | C4324 (intentional alignment padding) explicitly suppressed |\n| Compile-time asserts | SIZE power-of-two in [2, 2^30]; T noexcept move-constructible/assignable |\n\n## Interface\n\n```cpp\n// Shared between two threads:\nSPSCRing<AudioCommand, 1024> commands;\n\n// Main thread (producer):\nAudioCommand cmd = make_command(...);\nif (!commands.push(std::move(cmd))) {\n    // ring full — drop or handle backpressure\n}\n\n// Audio thread (consumer):\nAudioCommand out;\nwhile (commands.pop(out)) {\n    execute(out);\n}\n```\n\n```cpp\nstatic constexpr size_t capacity();   // SIZE - 1 usable slots\n\nbool push(T&&);                        // producer thread only\nbool push(const T&);                   // copy convenience overload\nbool pop(T& out);                      // consumer thread only; false = empty\n\nsize_t size_approx() const;            // monitoring only (non-atomic)\nbool   empty_approx() const;\nbool   full_approx()  const;\n```\n\n## Files changed\n\n- `core/templates/spsc_ring.h` — new file (168 lines including MIT header, full doc comments, static_asserts)\n\nDesigned and implemented by Matthew Busel.","labels":[{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-03-11T07:59:34Z","updated_at":"2026-03-11T09:26:26Z","closed_at":"2026-03-11T09:18:18Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"a4b61174e56ee137af4fdc0d8c7198b8627a940d","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"Mattbusel:feat/spsc-ring","ref":"feat/spsc-ring","repo":null,"sha":"2ffe41b5cebf88ed09419d2e2e2477639a73f321","user":{"login":"Mattbusel","id":183046053,"node_id":"U_kgDOCukPpQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/183046053?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mattbusel","html_url":"https://github.com/Mattbusel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mattbusel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mattbusel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mattbusel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mattbusel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mattbusel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mattbusel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mattbusel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mattbusel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Matt